 respect to the task at hand. When you are done, provide your final answer as a single result: for example, if asked for a number, simply return the number alone. If asked for the name of something, return only the name, and no additional text. Don't add any extra text to `terminate_with_result` beyond your answer. Do not overcomplicate the task; do what it asks for, and nothing more.\n\nDo not interact with the Advanced Reporting tab if you are using Magento Admin.\n",
  "formatted_code": "async def act(page):\n    # Get the orders table (fourth table in the document)\n    orders_table = page.get_by_role('table').nth(3)\n    # Get the data rows from the second rowgroup (index 1)\n    data_rows = orders_table.get_by_role('rowgroup').nth(1).get_by_role('row')\n    total_amount = 0.0\n    count = 0\n    # Iterate through rows\n    for i in range(await data_rows.count()):\n        row = data_rows.nth(i)\n        # Get the status cell (8th cell, index 7)\n        status_cell = row.get_by_role('cell').nth(7)\n        status_text = await status_cell.text_content()\n        if status_text and 'Complete' in status_text:\n            # Get the Grand Total (Purchased) cell (7th cell, index 6)\n            gt_cell = row.get_by_role('cell').nth(6)\n            gt_text = await gt_cell.text_content()\n            if gt_text:\n                # Remove currency symbol and commas, convert to float\n                amount = float(gt_text.replace('$', '').replace(',', '').strip())\n                total_amount += amount\n                count += 1\n                if count >= 5:\n                    break\n    # Return the total amount as a string\n    return str(total_amount)",
